      "extract": "The role of the projective line minus three points X = P1\\{0, 1, ∞} in relation to Galois theory can be traced back to Belyi’s theorem [4] (1979): Theorem 1.1. Every smooth projective algebraic curve deﬁned over Q can be realised as a ramiﬁed cover of P1, whose ramiﬁcation locus is contained in {0, 1, ∞}. Belyi deduced that the absolute Galois group of Q acts faithfully on the proﬁnite completion of the fundamental",
