      "extract": "Conjecture 3.2. A variant of Grothendieck’s period conjecture states that per : Pm MT (Z) −→C is injective. In particular, its restriction to H is injective also. The last statement, together with theorem 1.5, is equivalent to Conjecture 3.3. (Hoﬀman) The elements ζ(n1, . . . , nr) for ni ∈{2, 3} are a basis for the Q-vector space spanned by multiple zeta values. This in turn implies a conjecture due to Zagier,",
