      "extract": "Thus an Euler sum of weight N and depth r can be expressed as a polynomial in the above elements, of total weight N and total depth ≤r. 5. Depth The results of the previous section for N = 2, 3, 4, 6, 8 crucially use the fact that the depth ﬁltration is dual to the lower central series of the corresponding motivic Galois group. A fundamental diﬀerence with the case N = 1 is that this fact is false for P1\\{0, 1, ∞},",
