      "extract": "where UΓ is pro-unipotent. There is a natural map Γ →GΓ(k) which is Zariski dense, and whose projection onto S(k) is the map ρ. 2. In ‘geometric’ situations, one expects the relative completion to be the Betti realisation of something which is motivic. Indeed, Hain has shown [23], [24] that O(GΓ) carries a mixed Hodge structure in this case. As a result, one can deﬁne Hodge-motivic periods and try to carry out §1.4.",
